<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marikudo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marikudo is the Ati chief of Panay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragtas">Maragtas</a> legend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visayas">Visayas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. In the story he sold the lowlands of the island to ten datus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/datu-puti">Datu Puti</a>, for a golden salakot and a long gold necklace, and moved with his people into the hills. He is a figure of folklore rather than documented history.</p></div>
